    "### Part D — Correlation and Causality Answers\n",
    "1. **Does correlation guarantee a specific score?** \n",
    "   No. Correlation only measures the strength and direction of a linear relationship between variables. It does not guarantee an exact individual score because other factors (like test anxiety or prior knowledge) also play a role.\n",
    "2. **Potential Lurking / Confounding Variable:** \n",
    "   Student motivation or access to private tutoring could act as a confounding variable that independently drives both higher study hours and higher grades."
