    "### Part E — Vector Math Concepts\n",
    "1. **What does the weight vector ($w$) represent?** \n",
    "   Weights represent the relative importance or impact of each feature. A higher weight means that feature has a stronger influence on predicting the final score.\n",
    "2. **Why do we need bias ($b$)?** \n",
    "   Bias acts as a baseline shift (an intercept). It ensures that even if all input features were zero, the model can still predict a realistic baseline starting score."
