    "### Part F — Feature Scaling Justification\n",
    "**Why would a distance-based algorithm (like K-Nearest Neighbors) fail without scaling?**\n",
    "`study_hours` ranges roughly from 0 to 10, whereas `previous_mark` ranges from 30 to 110. In a distance formula (like Euclidean distance), features with much larger numerical ranges completely dominate the calculation. Without scaling, the model would be effectively blind to smaller-scaled features like study hours. Scaling puts all features on an equal mathematical playing field."
